cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Universal Honeypot Benchmarking Standard (UHBS)"
message: "If you use UHBS, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: standard
authors:
  - name: "UHBS Project Stewards"
    alias: "Spec / Harness / Security Stewards"
    website: "https://github.com/mziqudhd92/uhbs-standard"
  - name: "Moran Zavdi"
    email: "security@uhbs.dev"
    website: "https://github.com/mziqudhd92"
version: "4.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-26"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mziqudhd92/uhbs-standard"
url: "https://mziqudhd92.github.io/uhbs-standard/"
abstract: >-
  UHBS v4.0 is a vendor-neutral, objective, repeatable, and quantitative
  methodology for evaluating honeypots and deception technology. It defines six
  evaluation modules (A–F), a composite UHQS score (0–100) with production
  baseline UHQS > 80, a non-linear Safety Gate, machine-readable schemas, and a
  UHBS-Lab reference harness (uhbs_core) with a vendor-neutral conformance
  suite for reproducible UHQS verification.
keywords:
  - honeypot
  - deception-technology
  - cybersecurity
  - benchmarking
  - security-standard
  - OT
  - ICS
  - GenAI
